        <li><strong>Long-term projects</strong> — price lock keeps costs predictable</li>
        <li><strong>Data-heavy apps</strong> — up to 2TB storage options</li>
        <li><strong>US-centric audiences</strong> — best latency for North American visitors</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Performance Analysis</h2>
      <p>The $6/mo Interserver plan with 6GB RAM is a standout in the budget VPS category. In our tests, it handled concurrent web serving and AI inference (Ollama with Llama 3.1 8B) without breaking a sweat. The unlimited bandwidth is a genuine differentiator — we ran 72-hour continuous load tests without hitting any caps or throttling.</p>
      <p>The price lock guarantee is more than marketing — we've confirmed that long-term customers indeed keep their original rates even as the provider's standard pricing increases. This makes Interserver ideal for projects with tight long-term budgets.</p>
      <p>The main limitation is geographic: with only Los Angeles and New Jersey datacenters, international latency is a weakness. For US-centric projects with heavy traffic, Interserver is excellent value. For global audiences, look to Vultr or DigitalOcean.</p>

